    {
      "id": 28,
      "title": "Multi-Principal Routing Topology & Governance Invariants",
      "description": "Architectural reference for principal isolation, tool registry partitioning, and budget ledger.",
      "type": "text",
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 6,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 65
      },
      "options": {
        "mode": "markdown",
        "content": "### Governed Multi-Principal Architecture\n\n```text\n                     Root Orchestrator (orchestrator)\n                     \u2502  \u2022 ToolRegistry: [delegate_task, create_file (CONFIRM REQUIRED)]\n                     \u2502  \u2022 HierarchicalBudgetLedger (Anti-Multiplication Authority)\n                     \u2502\n          \u250c\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2534\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2500\u2510\n          \u25bc delegate_task                      \u25bc delegate_task\n   workspace_analyst                    transport_specialist\n   \u2022 ToolRegistry: [read_file,          \u2022 ToolRegistry: [find_connection (MCP)]\n                    list_dir, search]   \u2022 Conversational Context: Isolated\n   \u2022 Conversational Context: Isolated   \u2022 Budget Slice: max_steps <= remaining_parent\n   \u2022 Budget Slice: Sliced & Reconciled  \u2022 Enforcement: Shared PermissionManager\n```\n\n**Security Invariants**: Sub-agents receive fresh, role-specific `ToolExecutor` instances with least-privilege tool subsets. Conversational history does not leak from parent turns, and budget cannot multiply across descendants."
      }
    },
